# Installer automatic self-heal

> **ABSOLUTE**: `install.ps1` / `install.sh` (and site public copies) must recover a broken install without requiring manual per-machine environment cleanup.

## Required on every install run

1. Stop running `ax` processes (best effort).
2. Clear stuck upgrade leftovers (`upgrade-status.txt`, `upgrade-staging-*`) under the product install root.
3. Clear invalid `AX_VERSION` pins (Process + User) when the pin has no platform asset; install the latest installable release instead.
4. On GitHub API 401/403 from `GITHUB_TOKEN`/`GH_TOKEN`, retry without Authorization and unset those tokens for the install process (clear User/Machine only after confirmed auth failure, with a warning).

## Forbidden

- Documenting a separate “geheim” env-cleanup ritual as the required fix path for these failure modes.
- Using HTTP HEAD against GitHub release CDN URLs.
- Touching project `.ax` databases (product install tree only).